As per the police report, it is, inter-alia, stated by Janardan Singh in his statement that he worked as a security guard and has two children, namely, daughter Vandana (elder) and son Alok Singh;
that he had got his daughter Vandana married to Ashu Saini son of Prem Chander Saini according to the Hindu rites and customs; that from the marriage itself, her mother-in-law, namely, Veena Saini had used to taunt her for not bringing dowry and other articles and that her parents were pauper;
that mother-in-law and husband of his daughter had always used to beat his daughter and demanding her to bring money and jewellary from her parents and also used to harass her mentally and physically; that her daughter had told him that her jewellary articles had been taken away by her husband and mother-in-law and she had been kept inside house; that on 03.02.2016, her daughter gave birth to a male child at her parents' village.

The essential ingredients of the offence under section 304B are as follows:
(i) the death of a woman must have been caused by burns or bodily injury or otherwise than under normal circumstances;
(ii) such death must have occurred within seven years of her marriage;
(iii) soon before her death, the woman must have been subjected to cruelty or harassment by her husband or any relatives of her husband;
State vs Ashutosh Saini @ Ashu Anr on 3 February, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/186644509/
15

To bring home the guilt of the accused the prosecution is to establish the following:
(1) that the accused is the husband or the relative of the husband of the woman in question;
(2) that the said woman was subjected to cruelty by her husband and/or his relative.
